# Pairs with EventualConvergence in ReplicationReBootstrap. Detaching a peer skips its shipper past
# the log (#4534-B); re-attaching it must re-seed it, or what was skipped is lost.
MODULE: EventualConvergenceReattachWithoutReseed
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a detached peer is re-attached without a re-seed, so the entries its detached shipper skipped never arrive
PERTURBS: Detach

--- FIND
    /\ detached' = TRUE
    /\ fellOff' = TRUE
--- REPLACE
    /\ detached' = TRUE
\* MUTATION: re-attaching requests no re-seed.
    /\ fellOff' = fellOff
--- END
